#####################################################################
# cp32_brick_hex_default_mo.lgi
#
# group    : brick
# expect   : valid
# spec     : brick xyz 9,5,9 0.,0.,0. 1.,1.,1. 1,1,1
# points   : out_cp32_pts.inp
# mesh     : out_cp32_pts.inp hex
#
# WHAT:
#   the hex brick in a mesh object made with NO cell type (tet by
#   default), as LaGriT's own tests do (level01 filter, quality,
#   surface): brick sets the cell type itself (rzbrick3.f), so this is
#   the same mesh as in a hex mesh object: 405 vertices, 256 hexes.
#   Refused by FIX 2 (Oct 13); allowed again by FIX 3 (user, Oct 16).
#
# FOUND (sandbox build; FIX 1-3 = createpts_lg.f, rzbrickg.f):
#   FIX 2 (Oct 13) to FIX 3 (Oct 16): ERROR 'the mesh object must
#   be hex'. Original code: the same AVS file as a hex mesh object.
#####################################################################
cmo / create / mo_default
createpts / brick / xyz / 9,5,9 / 0.,0.,0. / 1.,1.,1. / 1,1,1
dump / avs / out_cp32_pts.inp / mo_default
quality
finish
